{%- comment -%}
  Prints a residence's status word exactly as it reads on the site.

  Source of truth: Products › the residence › Status (metafield
  custom.status — a dropdown: For Sale, Under Offer, Coming Soon, Sold
  Prior to Completion, Sold; the list of choices is editable at
  Settings › Custom data › Products › Status).

  Residences without a Status fall back to the old "sold" tag, so nothing
  changes until the field is filled in. Any status containing "Sold" sits
  in the Sold group; everything else is live (listed under For Sale).

  Usage: {% capture st %}{% render 'residence-status', product: p %}{% endcapture %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign st = product.metafields.custom.status.value | default: '' | strip
  if st == blank
    if product.tags contains 'sold'
      assign st = 'Sold Prior to Completion'
    else
      assign st = 'For Sale'
    endif
  endif
  echo st
-%}
